# kind | name | source (on-disk LICENSE path for shards; for clib/runtime, an
# SPDX id of licenses-spdx/, or the path of the library's own license file)
#
# Only what the released binary actually embeds. crystalreleaser has no runtime
# shard at all (stdlib only), and ameba is a development dependency that never
# ends up in it.
#
# The clib list follows the stdlib modules the tool requires:
#   Regex                      -> pcre2
#   YAML                       -> libyaml
#   Compress::Gzip/Zip         -> zlib
#   HTTP::Client over TLS      -> openssl (libssl + libcrypto)
#   GC, static libc, runtime   -> boehm-gc, musl, libgcc
# CONFIRMED on 2026-11-17 against the link line of this very binary, captured
# with `crystal build --static --verbose` in 84codes/crystal:1.20.3-alpine
# (the same libraries as on 2026-11-12, when it was built with -Dpreview_mt):
#   -lssl -lcrypto -lgc -lpcre2-8 -lpthread -lyaml -lz  (+ musl, libgcc)
# No gmp, no libevent. Licenses as apk records them in that image: openssl
# 3.5.7 Apache-2.0, pcre2 10.47 BSD-3-Clause, yaml 0.2.5 MIT, zlib 1.3.2 Zlib,
# musl 1.2.6 MIT. Re-run the check when a stdlib module is added or the
# image moves.
#
# MIT, BSD-3-Clause and zlib require the copyright notice to be reproduced,
# and their SPDX text only has a blank there: those four libraries embed their
# own license file, taken on 2026-11-12 from their sources at the versions
# above (to be taken again when a version moves):
#   pcre2    LICENCE.md  github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2  tag pcre2-10.47
#   libyaml  License     github.com/yaml/libyaml        tag 0.2.5
#   zlib     LICENSE     github.com/madler/zlib         tag v1.3.2
#   musl     COPYRIGHT   git.musl-libc.org/cgit/musl    tag v1.2.6
clib    | openssl         | Apache-2.0
clib    | pcre2           | licenses-upstream/pcre2.txt
clib    | libyaml         | licenses-upstream/libyaml.txt
clib    | zlib            | licenses-upstream/zlib.txt
clib    | boehm-gc        | Boehm-GC
clib    | musl            | licenses-upstream/musl.txt
clib    | libgcc          | GCC-runtime-exception
runtime | crystal         | Apache-2.0
project | crystalreleaser | LICENSE
